> because the 'eclipse.application' in 'configuration/config.ini' was
> empty. Right now, I use org.eclipse.ui.ide.workbench as value for that.
> Could this be the cause? Can you give me a hint/pointer on how to
> restore the javax/servlet again for R Help?

Do you mean, it still does not work after you removed the mentioned 
plugin? Did you already tried to use the Installation History of Eclipse 
[1]?
If this doesn't work, you have to find out the add-on (feature), which 
adds an additional version of javax.servlet.http, likely in a plug-in 
named javax.servlet. The default version in Eclipse 3.7 is 2.5.0.

I will add an additional dependency to try to prevent such version 
confusion in future versions of StatET (but an update for Eclipes 3.7 is 
not planned).

Regards,
Stephan


