Hi Mehdi,

Mehdi Lallouache wrote [2013-05-20 11:43]:
> Dear StatET users,
>
> I am a Ph.D student and I am currenctly using the great data.table
> package which introduce the syntax *:=*
>
> For eclipse, it is a syntax error, but it is not the case in the context
> of this package.
>
> Is there a way to make Eclipse consider *:=* as correct ?

At moment, no. StatET parses and checks the R code in accordance with 
the "R Language Definition" [1] and AFAIK ":=" is not listed as valid 
operator. A workaround is to write it as function call.

Regards,
Stephan


>
> Many thanks
>
> Mehdi


[1] http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-lang.pdf

